** MMP9560 - COMPRESS/SEPARATE OPERAND-LIST CONTINUATION FIXTURE
** Sibling of MMP9550.nsp: COMPRESS/SEPARATE build the same kind of
** multi-operand list as WRITE/DISPLAY/PRINT (see natural.py's
** RE_COMPRESS_SEPARATE), so a continuation line opening with a bare field
** reference (CONTINUATION_LEAD_FIELD) must fold into them the same way it
** does for WRITE, not just when the line already carries the closing INTO
** keyword (MMP9800.nsp's own COMPRESS fixture only exercises that case).
DEFINE DATA LOCAL
1 #BATCH-SEQ (N4)
1 #MESSAGE (A60)
END-DEFINE
COMPRESS 'BATCH'
  #BATCH-SEQ
  INTO #MESSAGE
END
